 ],
 "stem": "If $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{{=p}}{{=q}}$, find the value of $\\frac{{=u}a+{=v}b}{b}$. Give the answer as a fraction in its simplest form (a whole number if it is one).",
 "answer": "{=n}/{=d}",
 "solution": [
  "Since $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{{=p}}{{=q}}$, let $a={=p}m$ and $b={=q}m$ with $m\\neq 0$.",
  "$\\frac{{=u}a+{=v}b}{b}=\\frac{{=u}\\times {=p}m+{=v}\\times {=q}m}{{=q}m}=\\frac{{=n0}m}{{=q}m}$.",
  "$=\\frac{{=n0}}{{=q}}$, which in simplest form is {=n}/{=d}."
 ],
 "marker": {
  "kind": "expression",
  "answer": "{=n}/{=d}",
  "form": "simplest",
  "variables": [],
  "tolerance": null
 },
 "proposed_misconceptions": [],
 "notes": "Basic: one substitution a=pm, b=qm, m cancels. gcd(p,q)=1 so a/b is in lowest terms; the final fraction is reduced by gcd(n0,q)."
}
